## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/randommono.html
- Summary (EN): Random Mono generates random values for a mono layer, VDB or attribute. By default the Seed-driven selection fills the whole layer, and per-pixel randomness creates fine, grain-like noise. Values can come from a Min/Max range, a Float Ramp or a Specific Values list.
- Résumé (FR) : Ce nœud génère des valeurs mono aléatoires pour un calque, un VDB ou un attribut, selon une plage, une rampe ou une liste de valeurs.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output image size and metadata", "min: layer or attribute setting the minimum limit when Range Values is Min/Max", "max: layer or attribute setting the maximum limit when Range Values is Min/Max", "ramp: layer or attribute sampled horizontally for range values when Range Values is Float Ramp", "seed: layer or attribute controlling the random value distribution"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type the node outputs", "Range Values: Min/Max, Float Ramp or Specific Values", "Minimum / Maximum: bounds of the random range in Min/Max mode", "Float Ramp: reshapes the uniformly distributed random value through a ramp", "Number of Values, Value, Weight, Value List: for Specific Values; Value List accepts ranges with steps, such as 0-1:0.25", "Random per Pixel: selection varies per pixel", "Seed and Time: both change the random outcome", "Zero Negative IDs: when a seed input is wired, outputs 0 wherever the seed is a negative integer"]

- Caveats: ["Per-pixel randomness must be enabled explicitly, or the seed input must be used, to vary randomness for each custom shape.", "Within a Value List, all expanded values share the same weight.", "Sets with lower weights are selected less often; equal weights give equal probability.", "The page does not describe the Signature parameter beyond its brief definition."]

